# Default reviewers
#
# The paths below still carve out the intended working-group split (schemas,
# safety, HAL) for when the project has more than one maintainer — restore
# the `@openral/<wg>` teams once they exist. Until then every path routes to
# the sole maintainer.
#
# With one maintainer the branch ruleset requires 0 approvals (a PR author
# cannot approve their own PR, so 1 would force a ruleset bypass on every
# merge); the maintainer's merge is the review, since nobody else has write
# access. The day a second account gets write access, set the ruleset back to
# 1 approval + `require_code_owner_review`, which makes this file load-bearing
# again (docs/contributing/development.md, "Review policy").
*                                   @AdrianLlopart

# Schemas and IDL — extra care
python/core/**                      @AdrianLlopart
packages/msgs/**                    @AdrianLlopart

# Safety — mandatory review by safety WG
packages/openral_safety/**          @AdrianLlopart
cpp/openral_safety_kernel/**        @AdrianLlopart

# HAL adapters
packages/openral_hal_*/**           @AdrianLlopart

# CI / release
.github/**                          @AdrianLlopart
